d 'XHDFE': module to estimate high-dimensional fixed effects regression via a c++ plugin
d
d      xhdfe estimates linear models with high-dimensional fixed
d effects (HDFE) using a    C++ backend.  It mirrors the reporting
d and defaults of reghdfe where possible,    while exposing
d fixest-style small-sample corrections and ideas from pyfixest,   
d FixedEffectModels.jl, the within solvers of Fischer and
d Schroeder, and fereg by    Schmieder.  The command supports
d multiway fixed effects,    weights, robust and multiway-cluster
d inference, reghdfe-style singleton dropping    and DoF
d adjustments, and (optionally) the group()/individual() machinery. 
d KW: high-dimensional fixed effects
d KW: mulkti-way vlustering
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261125
d
d Author: Miguel Portela, Universidade do Minho
d Support: email miguel.portela@@eeg.uminho.pt
d
d Author: Tiago Tavares, Universidade do Minho
d Support: email tgstavares@@eeg.uminho.pt
d
